# Lead lens sign-off — cli#254 CI token wire
- date: 2026-09-27
- branch: feat/254-ci-token-wire
- lead: jerome-saltzer-and-michael-schroeder
- findings-status: no findings (YAML syntax valid; env vars pass through
  documented anticorruption layer; permissions block narrows default token)
- least-privilege verdict:
  - GITHUB_TOKEN narrowed to `contents: read` + `actions: read` at
    workflow level. No cross-repo write via default token.
  - SMOKE_GH_TOKEN referenced via ${{ secrets.SMOKE_GH_TOKEN }} — enters
    the process only through GitHub's masking pipeline. Never echoed.
  - docker run passes only 5 explicit -e vars (CLI_VERSION + 2 auth
    tokens + GH_TOKEN + GH_SMOKE_REPO). No bare --env, no --env-file.
  - Fork PRs without SMOKE_GH_TOKEN set: env value is empty string,
    passed as `GH_TOKEN=""` to container. In-container V2i logic
    treats empty as unset and skips Class 3 skills.
- sign-off: GO.
